        "new_information": [
          "On August 21, 2026, the Civil Aeronautics Administration (CAA) of Taiwan announced that booking for the second wave of extra flights and larger aircraft for the Mid-Autumn Festival and Teachers' Day holidays to Penghu and Kinmen will open on August 26 at 9:00 AM.",
          "The second-wave holiday flights will provide 7,384 seats in total, with 4,920 seats for the Penghu route and 2,464 seats for the Kinmen route.",
          "On August 20, 2026, the CAA announced that ticket bookings for the Retrocession Day holiday flights on offshore island routes (Penghu, Kinmen, and Matsu) will open on August 24 at 9:00 AM.",
          "The Retrocession Day holiday transport period is scheduled from October 23 to October 27, 2026, offering 1,072 flights and 87,268 seats across the three offshore island routes.",
          "For peak-hour flights during both holiday periods, tickets departing from Taiwan and returning from offshore islands are restricted to the designated date and flight, and are subject to tiered refund fees.",
          "On August 3, 2026, the CAA announced that passenger fuel surcharges for international flights operated by domestic airlines would increase starting August 9 due to rising aviation fuel prices."
        ]
